    "title": "Wordle",
    "image": "wordle.png",
    "href": "/g/wordle",
    "description": "Engage your lexicon and logic in Wordle, the daily word-guessing puzzle that has taken the world by storm. Your mission is simple: find the secret five-letter word in six attempts or less. Use the color-coded feedback—Green for correct position, Yellow for correct letter, Gray for wrong letter—to narrow down the possibilities and solve the daily mystery. With its elegant design and satisfying 'aha!' moment, Wordle offers a perfect daily mental workout that rewards vocabulary and strategic thinking. Track your streak and join a global community of puzzle enthusiasts.\n\nHow to Play & Tips:\n- Use 'Starter' words: Words with many vowels and common consonants (like ADIEU, ROATE, or STARE) are the best way to eliminate a large portion of the alphabet in your first two guesses.\n- Don't reuse Gray letters: It sounds obvious, but many people waste a guess on a word that contains letters they already know are wrong. Pay close attention to your keyboard status!\n- Think about letter frequency: If you have a 'Y', it's almost certainly at the end of the word. If you have a 'Q', look for a 'U' next to it.",
