    "description": "Test your patience and precision in the aptly named 'World's Hardest Game', a minimalist puzzle that demands total mastery of movement. Control a small red square as you navigate through a series of labyrinthine levels filled with relentless blue enemies on set patrol routes. Your mission is simple: collect every yellow coin and reach the green exit zone without touching a single adversary. With its instant resets and escalating difficulty, it's a pure test of timing, pattern recognition, and nerves of steel that has fascinated and frustrated gamers for years.\n\nHow to Play & Tips:\n- Learn the patrol cycles: Blue dots always move in a fixed loop; sit at a checkpoint and count the seconds between gaps to find your opening.\n- Use 'Safe Spots': Checkpoints (green zones) are your best friend—some levels have dozens of dots but only one or two places where you are truly safe; find them first.\n- Move precisely: Use short, sharp arrow key presses to nudge your square—holding a key for too long often leads to over-correcting and hitting a dot.",
