      "image": "animal-crossing.webp",
      "href": "/g/animal-crossing",
      "description": "**Animal Crossing** is a beloved social simulation game series developed by Nintendo, where players immerse themselves in a charming village inhabited by anthropomorphic animals. The gameplay is open-ended, allowing players to engage in activities such as fishing, insect catching, fossil hunting, and decorating their homes. A standout feature of the series is its real-time gameplay, which mirrors the actual passage of time, including seasons and holidays, enhancing the immersive experience. \n\nThe latest installment, *Animal Crossing: New Horizons*, has received a significant update coinciding with the release of the Nintendo Switch 2 Edition. This update introduces enhanced visuals with 4K resolution in TV mode, mouse-like Joy-Con 2 controls, and expanded online gameplay supporting up to 12 players. New features include the addition of a Resort Hotel managed by Kapp'n’s family, where players can decorate themed rooms and earn exclusive items. The update also brings back the character Resetti with a new Reset Service to assist in organizing the island. Quality of life improvements such as increased home storage up to 9,000 items and the ability to craft from storage have also been implemented. \n\nFor players who enjoy creative and social simulation games, titles like [Grow A Garden](/class/Grow-A-Garden) and [Monkey Mart](/class/Monkey-Mart) offer engaging experiences. In *Grow A Garden*, players cultivate their own virtual gardens, while *Monkey Mart* allows players to manage a bustling marketplace, both providing delightful and immersive gameplay.\n\n*Animal Crossing: New Horizons* continues to captivate players with its charming world and engaging activities, making it a standout title in the social simulation genre.\n\nHow to Play:\n- - W, A, S, D to move\n- - Space to jump\n- - Left Mouse Click to interact\n- - E to open inventory\n- - R to use tool",
