      "title": "Doom 1",
      "image": "doom-1.webp",
      "href": "/g/doom-1",
      "description": "**Doom 1** is a groundbreaking first-person shooter that revolutionized the gaming industry upon its release in 1993. Developed by id Software, it introduced players to fast-paced, immersive gameplay set in a science fiction and horror-themed universe. As the unnamed space marine, later known as \"Doomguy,\" players navigate through military bases on Mars' moons and into the depths of Hell, battling hordes of demons and undead creatures. The game's innovative use of 3D graphics and networked multiplayer capabilities set a new standard for the genre. \n\nKey features of Doom 1 include a vast arsenal of weapons, ranging from the iconic shotgun to the powerful BFG 9000, and a variety of enemy types that require strategic combat approaches. The game's level design encourages exploration, with numerous secret areas and power-ups to discover. Its modding community has remained active over the years, contributing to its enduring popularity.\n\nIn recent years, the Doom franchise has seen significant updates and re-releases. For instance, the 2024 update for Doom and Doom II introduced 21:9 resolution support, enhanced audio options, and improved multiplayer features, bringing the classic experience to modern platforms. \n\nFor fans of intense, action-packed gameplay, titles like [Ultrakill](/class/Ultrakill) and [COD Zombies Portable](/class/COD-Zombies-Portable) offer similar adrenaline-fueled experiences. Additionally, [Hollow Knight](/class/Hollow-Knight) provides a challenging adventure with rich lore and engaging combat mechanics.\n\nDoom 1's legacy continues to influence the gaming world, inspiring countless titles and maintaining a dedicated fanbase eager to relive the classic demon-slaying action.\n\nHow to Play:\n- - W, A, S, D to move\n- - Space to jump\n- - Left Mouse Click to fire\n- - Right Mouse Click to use\n- - E to open doors, activate switches, and use items",
