      "title": "Orb Farm",
      "image": "orb-farm.jpg",
      "href": "/g/orb-farm",
      "description": ": Cultivate Your Own Digital Ecosystem\n\nOrb Farm is an engaging life simulation game that allows players to create and manage a miniature ecosystem. By introducing various elements such as water, algae, stone, grass, wood, and sand, players can design a balanced environment where life forms interact and thrive. The game challenges users to maintain equilibrium between oxygen (O₂) and carbon dioxide (CO₂) levels, fostering the growth of diverse organisms. \n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Dynamic Ecosystem Simulation**: Observe the intricate relationships between different life forms as they interact within your custom-built environment.\n\n- **Environmental Management**: Adjust environmental parameters like pH, CO₂, O₂ levels, and temperature to create optimal conditions for your ecosystem.\n\n- **Intuitive Controls**: Easily manipulate elements within your ecosystem using simple touch or mouse controls, making the game accessible to players of all ages.\n\n- **Automatic Saving**: The game automatically saves your progress, allowing you to seamlessly continue your ecosystem management without the fear of losing data.\n\nFor those who enjoy simulation games that involve ecosystem management and creativity, Orb Farm offers a unique and educational experience. Players interested in similar simulation experiences might also enjoy [Grow A Garden](/class/Grow-A-Garden), where you can cultivate and manage a virtual garden, or [Idle Ants](/class/Idle-Ants), which allows you to oversee and expand an ant colony.\n\nOrb Farm is available to play online, providing a convenient and immersive platform for users to explore the complexities of ecological balance and the beauty of life simulation.\n\nHow to Play:\n- - Left Click to interact\n- - Right Click to delete items\n- - Shift + Right Click to remove all of a specific item type\n- - Scroll Wheel to zoom in/out\n- - Spacebar to pause/unpause simulation",
