      "title": "Super Mario 64",
      "image": "super-mario-64.webp",
      "href": "/g/super-mario-64",
      "description": "Super Mario 64 is a groundbreaking 3D platformer that revolutionized the gaming industry upon its release in 1996. Players control Mario as he navigates through Princess Peach's castle, entering various worlds via paintings to collect Power Stars and ultimately rescue the princess from Bowser. The game introduced a dynamic 360-degree analog control system, allowing for precise movements such as walking, running, jumping, and performing special maneuvers like the triple jump and wall kick. This level of control set a new standard for 3D platformers. \n\nIn addition to its innovative gameplay mechanics, Super Mario 64 features a health system represented by a pie chart with eight segments. Players can replenish health by collecting coins or interacting with specific in-game elements. The game also includes various power-ups and hidden secrets, encouraging exploration and replayability. Its open-world design and non-linear level progression have influenced countless titles in the genre. \n\nOver the years, Super Mario 64 has inspired numerous fan-made projects and mods. For instance, the Super Mario 64 Coop Deluxe mod allows up to 16 players to experience the game cooperatively, introducing new playable characters and modern features. This mod showcases the enduring appeal and adaptability of the original game. \n\nFor fans of classic platformers, titles like [Hollow Knight](/class/Hollow-Knight) and [Pizza Tower](/class/Pizza-Tower) offer engaging experiences with unique mechanics and art styles. Additionally, [Retro Bowl College](/class/Retro-Bowl-College) provides a nostalgic sports gaming experience reminiscent of retro titles.\n\nSuper Mario 64's legacy continues to thrive, with ongoing discoveries and community-driven content keeping the game relevant for both new players and longtime fans.\n\nHow to Play:\n- - Arrow Keys to move\n- - Space to jump\n- - X to run\n- - Z to crouch\n- - Enter to pause",
